 "verdict_explanation": "Every field the two keys share is a field GnuPG fills in by itself. Read straight out of gnupg-1.4.16 g10/keygen.c, the compiled-in default preference set with no gpg.conf override is exactly S9 S8 S7 S3 S2 / H8 H2 H9 H10 H11 / Z2 Z3 Z1 with mdc=1 and modify=0 -- i.e. the identical values both keys carry. The agreement therefore carries no discriminating information: it says only that both keys were made by running `gpg --gen-key` on a 1.4/2.0 build and not editing the preference list. Every field a HUMAN chose -- key size, expiry policy, whether to revoke -- differs between them.",
